; A lot bought at a total price, {{$10}} for 3 X, is named again by the
; per-unit price that lot shows, {$3.333333}, and the two cancel.  The
; per-unit price divided out of the total is rounded to the quantity's
; precision plus the price commodity's precision plus six digits, which
; turns 10/3 into exactly $3.333333; a typed {$3.333333} then names the
; same lot.  The amount parser ({{total}}) and the pool's exchange (@@)
; share that rounding rule, so it must survive any change to either.

2024/01/01 Buy at a total
    Assets:A        3 X {{$10}}
    Equity:Opening

2024/02/01 Sell by the displayed unit price
    Assets:A       -3 X {$3.333333}
    Equity:Opening

2024/03/01 Buy by the displayed unit price
    Assets:B        3 Y {$3.333333}
    Equity:Opening

2024/04/01 Sell at a total
    Assets:B       -3 Y {{$10}}
    Equity:Opening

; The pool rounds an @@ cost the same way, and dates the lot it makes.
2024/05/01 Buy at a total cost
    Assets:C        3 Z @@ $10
    Equity:Opening

2024/06/01 Sell by the displayed unit price
    Assets:C       -3 Z {$3.333333} [2024/05/01]
    Equity:Opening

test bal --lots Assets
end test

test bal --lots Assets -E
                   0  Assets
                   0    A
                   0    B
                   0    C
--------------------
                   0
end test
